#!/usr/bin/env zsh
# claude-channels-allowlist-patch: bypass the approved-channels allowlist so any --channels plugin registers
# usage: claude-channels-allowlist-patch [--check|--restore|--all|--reapply] [path-to-claude-binary]
# --reapply: install-hook-friendly patch — clears the stale marker on success,
#            but on a missing needle warns loudly, writes the marker, exits 0.
#
# Why: gateChannelServer gates every non-dev channel on an allowlist. Its
# plugin branch reads the effective list and, on no match, returns
#   {action:"skip",kind:"allowlist"}
# so the channel never registers. All three registration paths — first connect,
# reconnect, and the SDK channel_enable control request — are gated on that same
# call returning "register", so a skip is total.
#
# The effective allowlist is either managed-org allowedChannelPlugins or the
# tengu_harbor_ledger remote-config feature (default []). With telemetry disabled
# (DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1, DO_NOT_TRACK=1) the ledger read short-circuits to that
# empty default, so *no* plugin is ever allowlisted — not even the official
# telegram plugin. There is no user-scope settings key or slash command for this
# list (anthropics/claude-code#58152); the only self-serve path is the
# per-launch, dialog-gated --dangerously-load-development-channels flag.
#
# Flipping the guard condition to a constant-false skips the allowlist branch for
# every entry, so any server explicitly passed via --channels registers without
# the dev flag or startup dialog: `0&&…` short-circuits, block skipped.
#
# Scope: the plugin: branch only. The same function's server:-form arm skips on
# its own `else if(!<name>.dev)`, which this patch leaves in place, so
# `--channels server:foo` still needs the dev flag. The cyc alias passes a
# plugin: entry, so nothing needs that arm today.
#
# --check proves the needle applied; it does not prove the channel registered.
# For that, launch with --debug and grep the session's ~/.claude/debug/*.txt:
#   "Channel notifications registered" / "re-registered after reconnect"
#     -> the gate returned register
#   "Channel notifications skipped: … not on the approved channels allowlist"
#     -> the gate is still blocking
# Nothing is written without --debug. The blocked case's on-screen warning is a
# 12-second toast, and print mode (-p) never connects a channel at all, so
# neither is a usable check.
#
# Two bits of UI look like that answer and are not. Both are render-only, and
# both were measured against the debug log above on the same session:
#
# 1. The startup line
#      plugin telegram@claude-plugins-official · not on the approved channels allowlist
#    still renders after patching and is *not* failure. A separate warning
#    builder (`uAm` in 2.1.227) re-derives allowlist membership for display and
#    never calls the gate; its result is only mapped into JSX and nothing
#    branches on it, so it reads identically patched and unpatched. It is also
#    accurate: this patch bypasses the membership check, it does not add the
#    plugin to the list, so membership really is unchanged — only the
#    consequence it implies is wrong. It may sit behind "+1 more · /status".
#
# 2. /status's "Channels: Listening for messages from …" is the false positive
#    the other way round. It is built from the parsed --channels entries and
#    suppressed only by a non-firstParty provider, the tengu_harbor master gate,
#    or org policy; the allowlist is never consulted. Measured: it reads
#    "Listening for messages from plugin:telegram@…" in the very session whose
#    debug log says "skipped: … not on the approved channels allowlist".
#
# The guarded local is a minified name, not a stable one. 2.1.227 reminified the
# scope and renamed it `o` -> `i`, which silently dropped a fixed-byte needle and
# put the gate back with no signal beyond a marker nothing surfaced. So the
# needle slots the name and re-emits whatever it captured, absorbing the next
# rename: `if(!%s.dev){` -> `if(0&&%s.d){`.
#
# Length-preserving for any name length, which Bun single-file binaries require
# (they embed a byte-offset source trailer, so an edit must not change length):
# the slot re-emits its capture verbatim, and `.dev` -> `.d` gives back exactly
# the two bytes `if(` -> `if(0&&` takes. same_length=1 asserts that at startup.
#
# expect_matches=1 because the site is verified unique: `.dev){` occurs exactly
# once in each installed binary (257-325MB), so a second match means the pattern
# has broadened and the patch should refuse rather than guess.
# Complements claude-channels-patch, which flips the tengu_harbor master gate.

emulate -L zsh
setopt no_unset pipe_fail

local wrapper="${${(%):-%x}:A}"
local patch_name=claude-channels-allowlist-patch
local patch_label='--channels allowlist'
local needle='if(!%s.dev){'
local replace='if(0&&%s.d){'
local needle_kind=slots
local same_length=1
local expect_matches=1
local marker="$HOME/.cache/claude-channels-allowlist-patch.stale"
local missing_body=$'The guard was likely reshaped upstream (a rename alone is absorbed by\nthe %s slot); the allowlist gate will re-block --channels plugins until\nthe needle in claude-channels-allowlist-patch is updated.'
local missing_banner='--channels allowlist gate will re-block'

source "${wrapper:h}/_claude-patch-targets-lib"
source "$HOME/.config/zsh/functions/patch/_needle-patch-lib"
